  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildlife Without Borders-Western Hemisphere</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of the Centro de Formacion para la Sustentabilidad Moxviquil, A.C. is to improve the pedagogical competencies of teachers and environmental promoters working in and around natural protected areas (NPAs) in the states of Chiapas, Campeche, Guerrero, Oaxaca, Quintana Roo and Yucatan. The Recipient will implement the following activities : 1) deliver a Train the Trainers certificate course on the implementation of the Manual for the Development of Environmental Education Curriculum and the Manual for the Conservation of Birds to 24 environmental educators from southeast Mexico; 2) certified trainers will replicate the course for 96 teachers in their home states, 3) increase the capacities of 24 NGOs employees to implement participatory environmental education programs; 4) design and implement 10 environmental education strategies for 10 NPAs in southeast Mexico; and 5) develop an education program on the design and implementation of environmental awareness activities for 20 young environmental promoters in Chiapas.</narrative>
  </description>
